Optional EAP and SIP database tests
===================================

These tests can run without containers. They require built app_diameap and
app_sip extensions, their dictionaries, the EAP identity and MD5 plugins,
MariaDB/MySQL development libraries and a disposable MariaDB instance.
The exchange tests also require Python 3, OpenSSL and local TCP networking;
the SIP dispatch test uses the mariadb command-line client.

Use an isolated, temporary database instance, never an existing production
database: the fixtures create tables and the SIP tests modify user records.
The tests use a passwordless local-only account named fd_test and fixed test
credentials. Do not expose that account or the test database socket.

Create empty databases named fd_diameap and fd_sip in the disposable
instance, and a local account 'fd_test'@'localhost' with SELECT on fd_diameap
and SELECT, UPDATE on fd_sip. Import the following files, in order, as an
administrator of that instance:

  fd_diameap: extensions/app_diameap/diameap.sql, tests/test_diameap_db.sql
  fd_sip:     doc/app_sip.sql, tests/test_sip_db.sql

The accounting test is separately optional and needs its own PostgreSQL
database; see testappacct.c for its table and connection requirements.

From the repository root, configure and build with the optional tests enabled:

  cmake -S . -B test.database -DBUILD_APP_DIAMEAP=ON -DBUILD_APP_SIP=ON \
    -DBUILD_DICT_NASREQ=ON -DBUILD_DICT_EAP=ON -DBUILD_DICT_SIP=ON \
    -DBUILD_EAP_IDENTITY=ON -DBUILD_EAP_MD5=ON \
    -DTEST_DIAMEAP_MYSQL=ON -DTEST_DIAMEAP_EXCHANGE=ON \
    -DTEST_APP_SIP_MYSQL=ON -DTEST_APP_SIP_DISPATCH=ON
  cmake --build test.database --parallel 2
  FD_TEST_MYSQL_SOCKET=/path/to/disposable/mysql.sock \
    FD_TEST_MYSQL_DATABASE=fd_sip FD_TEST_MYSQL_USER=fd_test \
    ctest --test-dir test.database -R '^(test_diameap_mysql|test_diameap_exchange|test_sip_db|test_sip_dispatch)$' --output-on-failure

The test fixtures are not safe to reuse with application data.
